      "text": "Uxmal – Mérida"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e386a04b44dc0cc9891f7c79ddf1d636276688fdbab7186f0e9b58be22766945",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-15p2nra73sw1g2",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "Leave for Uxmal in the morning. This Maya city is one of the best places to see the architecture of the Puuc region. Its buildings stand out for their scale and elaborate decoration. Ancient roads known as sacbeob linked buildings within the city and connected Uxmal to other settlements.\n\nThe Puuc style features smooth lower walls and decorative friezes with patterns derived from traditional Maya huts. The Pyramid of the Magician and the Governor's Palace make use of the natural terrain to rise even higher above the surrounding buildings.\n\nAfter exploring the ruins, continue to Mérida. On a sightseeing tour, you will see the historic centre and the modern part of the city, learn about its colonial past and ride in a horse-drawn carriage along Mérida's main avenue.\n\nStay at a 4-star hotel."
    },
